# Template for the backup repository settings.
#
# deploy/install.sh writes the real file to $DATA_DIR/config/backup/backup.env
# (mode 600); deploy/backup.container reads it via EnvironmentFile. Never
# committed. RESTIC_PASSWORD is a real secret: it encrypts the whole
# repository, so if you move the repo offsite you MUST keep a copy of it
# somewhere other than the data disk (a password manager, on paper) -- without
# it the backups are unrecoverable.
#
# The local default is the repo directory mounted at /repo (host path from
# STACK_BACKUP_DIR in stack.conf). A same-disk repo survives accidental
# deletion but not the disk itself; for real disaster recovery point this at
# an offsite target, e.g. s3:s3.amazonaws.com/bucket/path,
# b2:bucket:path, or sftp:user@host:/srv/restic.
RESTIC_REPOSITORY=/repo
RESTIC_PASSWORD=change-me
# restic's cache inside the container (host dir $DATA_DIR/backup-cache).
RESTIC_CACHE_DIR=/cache
